    "appliesTo": "Full-time basic monthly salary, Singapore, 5-day week",
    "source": "JTE, November 2026",
    "short": "Below about S$2,500 basic a month, a job gets much harder to fill.",
    "long": "This is not a rule, just what we see. You can pay less. Expect to wait longer, and to lose people to the employer down the road. Everyone compares. For hands-on jobs on a 5-day week, S$2,500 is about where the market starts.",
    "exemptNote": "The S$2,500 mark is about basic pay, where the basic is the whole package. Many hands-on jobs pay a lower basic with overtime on top. Judge those on the gross. Where we know both, we show both."
  },
