      "floor": {
        "amount": 1800,
        "appliesTo": "Base monthly salary, Singapore community care and support roles",
        "source": "JTE, November 2026",
        "short": "Care jobs run on bands, not one rate. Care staff starts around S$2,500.",
        "long": "Care pay runs on bands. The entry level, a health attendant, starts at S$1,800. A healthcare assistant or care staff job starts around S$2,500 and goes to about S$3,200. Those are base figures, so overtime and shift allowances sit on top. Nursing is the one to watch. The base bands are real, but they are not what closes a hire. A clinic assistant already starts above S$2,500, and a nurse carries far more than that. Budget a starting gross of about S$3,000 or the job will stay open.",
        "displayAmount": 2500
      },
      "note": "Pay here depends on which band the job sits in, more than on years served. Tell us the duties and how much supervision there is, and we will tell you the band."
